From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:30:39 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0201): mac-windows key translation and escape chord
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DEC-6 / DEC-22, PLAN §6.1; AC-11, AC-12, AC-13, AC-35, AC-59.

Translation runs on the controller, on the key events upstream already
built for the peer, so the host stays stock. New module
src/remotesmith_keymap.rs (declared from keyboard.rs):

- Translated mode, per peer option remotesmith-translate-shortcuts
  (empty/Y = on when Mac<->Windows, N = raw): Mac -> Windows Cmd->Ctrl,
  Ctrl->Ctrl, Option->Alt, Cmd+Tab->Alt+Tab; Windows -> Mac Ctrl->Cmd,
  Win->Ctrl, Alt->Option, Alt+Tab->Cmd+Tab. Map, translate and legacy
  key events and mouse modifier flags. Raw mode is upstream's map mode.
- Escape chord Ctrl+Option+Cmd+Esc / Ctrl+Alt+Win+Esc, matched on
  physical keys before any mapping in both modes: Esc is never
  forwarded, every held key is released on the host, the grab is
  dropped and the page is told to give up focus. Session stays up.
- Mode changes and capture loss release everything the translation
  holds on the host; capture loss also forgets local modifier state,
  so the next press of a modifier is not taken for a repeat.
- The grab loop now sends through the current session
  (process_event -> process_session_event) so both input sources get
  the same handling; upstream's Cmd/Ctrl swap is bypassed while the
  translation is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
